{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VYJ1dz87TvvwSaGfk8ytSX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/blog/2024/10/23/how-to-ace-kcna-kubernetes-and-cloud-native-associate-exam/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"NOT AUTHORITATIVE — community guest post syndicated onto the CNCF blog. Retained solely as evidence of what third parties claim.\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Provenance of the \"60 questions / 75%\" figures\n10\t\n11\t> DO NOT CITE THE CONTENTS OF THIS FILE AS FACT. This snapshot exists to\n12\t> document WHERE a widely-repeated claim comes from, which is itself the\n13\t> subject of Chapter 1 §2. It is not a source for the claim's truth.\n14\t\n15\t## The claim, as it appears\n16\t\n17\t\"You'll have 90 minutes to answer 60 questions\" and \"the passing score is >75%\"\n18\t\n19\tThe same post states the pre-change five-domain blueprint as:\n20\t\"Kubernetes Fundamentals 46% / Container Orchestration 22% / Cloud Native\n21\tArchitecture 16% / Cloud Native Observability 8% / Cloud Native Application\n22\tDelivery 8%\"\n23\t\n24\t## Why this is not authoritative\n25\t\n26\tThe byline reads: \"Community post originally published on Medium by Giorgi\n27\tKeratishvili\". It is a syndicated community contribution hosted on cncf.io, not\n28\ta CNCF publication. Hosting on the authority's domain is what lends the figures\n29\ttheir apparent authority.\n30\t\n31\t## Cross-check against authoritative sources (all fetched 2026-08-23)\n32\t\n33\t- 90 minutes — CONFIRMED published (LF exam page; LF MC FAQ).\n34\t- 75% passing score — CONFIRMED published (LF MC FAQ, for MC exams as a class).\n35\t- 60 questions — NOT FOUND in any authoritative source. Checked and absent from:\n36\t  the LF KCNA exam page; the LF MC exam FAQ; the LF general certification FAQ;\n37\t  the LF exam-results handbook page; the CNCF KCNA page; the LFS250 outline.\n38\t- 46/22/16/8/8 — NOT independently sourced. See\n39\t  cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md (open gap).\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9534cc4f-be85-4d73-8a35-cd0d846700e5","uuid":"f0decd74-212a-4823-8fd3-47f0f10beb65","timestamp":"2026-08-31T09:36:52.521Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/blog/2024/10/23/how-to-ace-kcna-kubernetes-and-cloud-native-associate-exam/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"NOT AUTHORITATIVE — community guest post syndicated onto the CNCF blog. Retained solely as evidence of what third parties claim.\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n---\n\n# Provenance of the \"60 questions / 75%\" figures\n\n> DO NOT CITE THE CONTENTS OF THIS FILE AS FACT. This snapshot exists to\n> document WHERE a widely-repeated claim comes from, which is itself the\n> subject of Chapter 1 §2. It is not a source for the claim's truth.\n\n## The claim, as it appears\n\n\"You'll have 90 minutes to answer 60 questions\" and \"the passing score is >75%\"\n\nThe same post states the pre-change five-domain blueprint as:\n\"Kubernetes Fundamentals 46% / Container Orchestration 22% / Cloud Native\nArchitecture 16% / Cloud Native Observability 8% / Cloud Native Application\nDelivery 8%\"\n\n## Why this is not authoritative\n\nThe byline reads: \"Community post originally published on Medium by Giorgi\nKeratishvili\". It is a syndicated community contribution hosted on cncf.io, not\na CNCF publication. Hosting on the authority's domain is what lends the figures\ntheir apparent authority.\n\n## Cross-check against authoritative sources (all fetched 2026-08-23)\n\n- 90 minutes — CONFIRMED published (LF exam page; LF MC FAQ).\n- 75% passing score — CONFIRMED published (LF MC FAQ, for MC exams as a class).\n- 60 questions — NOT FOUND in any authoritative source. Checked and absent from:\n  the LF KCNA exam page; the LF MC exam FAQ; the LF general certification FAQ;\n  the LF exam-results handbook page; the CNCF KCNA page; the LFS250 outline.\n- 46/22/16/8/8 — NOT independently sourced. See\n  cncf-curriculum-repo-kcna-versions-2026-08-23.md (open gap).\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
